  "title": "EEOC and DOJ Warn Employers: DEI Programs Must Comply with Anti-Discrimination Laws",
  "summary": "This latest guidance from the EEOC and DOJ is not a rejection of DEI goals—it’s a reminder that equality under the law must guide how those goals are pursued. Employers can still promote inclusion, equity, and belonging, but they must do so in ways that comply with Title VII and avoid discriminatory practices, regardless of intent.",
